{
  "description": "Resolution and composition. 'overlays' maps identity to manifest; 'files' lists an overlay's files, from which the fields a manifest does not write take their defaults (skills, rules, context, paths). A 'files' entry may instead map each path to its text, for the files read as env files. 'expect' gives the visiting order, the composition order and what the active overlays contribute, or the cycle; with 'facts', the environment they build together, or the refusal. 'facts' may give 'packages' (per identity, each runtime's installed packages directory) and 'removed' (overlays being removed); a case that states 'environments' also expects the dependency environments (runtime, environment, overlays in composition order, files, locked), the 'conflicts' (runtime, environment, package, overlays), the overlays 'blocked' by them (not activated, absent from 'active' and the environment), and what each removed overlay 'left' ('rebuilt' or 'deleted').",
  "spec": "spec/v0/composition.md",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "order-priority-name",
      "description": "Ascending (priority, name, identity); requires does not change the order.",
      "overlays": {
        "engineering": {
          "name": "engineering",
          "routing": [
            "- eng"
          ]
        },
        "python": {
          "requires": [
            "engineering"
          ],
          "routing": [
            "- py"
          ],
          "priority": 300
        },
        "team": {
          "name": "Alpha",
          "priority": 700,
          "routing": [
            "- team"
          ],
          "context": [
            "CONTEXT.md"
          ]
        },
        "zeta": {
          "name": "",
          "routing": [
            "- zeta"
          ]
        }
      },
      "requested": [
        "team",
        "python",
        "zeta"
